<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

Terra-B10: Lares (Tasked Spirit), a build seat in /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt (branch feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5&#45;-b1-lift, head 07f0785c7). Never commit, build, run browser-mode vitest, or open a socket.

Two exact jobs, the witness cell of CI 42227482250:
# MEET B10 (never dodge it: never rename the test to drop its "stands" word, never add an allowance): tools/barrier-witness.mjs reads five `holds` assertions in packages/lararium-web/tests/e2e/glass-tabs.e2e.test.ts at lines 62, 66, 74, 75, 81 with no named far-side barrier before them. Read tools/barrier-witness.mjs whole (how it recognizes a named barrier) and the precedent diff /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/terra-b10/b10-precedent.diff (83ca74cca met B10 in the glass promotion e2e: each held-value read follows the last act and its named barrier marker). In glass-tabs, each read waits on a real far-side event (the tab's mirror word through `settled(...)`, the floor-tab role through the page): make each assertion follow the act it observes and name that barrier the way the witness reads it. Edit ONLY that e2e file. Verify: `node tools/barrier-witness.mjs` reads backlog 0/0.
# THE INVENTORY: run `node tools/capability-inventory.mjs --write` from the worktree root (it measures the source and rewrites tools/capability-inventory.json); then `bash tools/capability-inventory-witness.sh` (or `node --test tools/capability-inventory.test.mjs`) reads green. Edit nothing else.
Write out.md: per job the diff summary and the witness result.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/seat-law`>>

!! SEAT LAW (appended by tools/launch-codex.mjs to every brief; it binds this seat)
* A lane launches no Sol seat; the controller's one Sol read per train runs at the read floor of 0%.
* Stay inside the wall. Approval never escalates; a build seat has no network, loopback included; only a research seat takes `--search`. A step that needs more than the wall stops and names itself in `out.md`; the wall holds by refusal.
* Never commit and never run a git write. The lead commits each red, then each fix.
* Never build (`pnpm build`), never run vitest browser mode, never stand a vessel, socket or daemon. Typecheck (`tsc -p … --noEmit`) and run single test files that open no socket; mark any test that needs a socket "lead runs".
* A "stale build" from the dist guard stops the run; name it, and the lead builds.
* A read seat writes no file: its final message carries the hand-back. Any other seat writes `out.md` and every note in the seat directory alone. `-o` names `final.md`; stdin closes (`< /dev/null`); `TMPDIR` and `TMPPREFIX` sit inside the seat directory.
* Never run the battery; the lead holds its lock. Never read a credential file.
* Launch without `--ephemeral`: each seat keeps its rollout, so the spend tally counts it.
* The lead runs `pnpm build` in its worktree after every span merge and before each build seat; a verdict read off a stale dist counts as unread.

<<~/ahu>>

